  "reasoning": "The patient presents with a triad of high fever, significant weakness, and muscle pain. While several conditions on the list can cause fever, the combination of severe muscle pain (classically associated with 'breakbone fever') and profound weakness strongly points to dengue. Malaria typically presents with cyclical chills, sweating, and headaches, which are absent here. Typhoid usually features prominent abdominal pain rather than isolated muscle pain. Based on the reference patterns linking acute fever, muscle/body pain, and weakness to dengue, this is the most accurate diagnosis.",
  "final_answer": "[DIAGNOSIS]dengue[/DIAGNOSIS]"
